mkclass() is from makemon.c and it does this:
            if (!(mvitals[last].mvflags & G_GONE) && !(mons[last].geno & mask)
                                        && !is_placeholder(&mons[last])) {

G_GONE is (G_GENOD|G_EXTINCT) (monflag.h); G_EXTINCT is set by propagate()
in makemon.c.

Cleric insect summoning respects extinction.

It also calls makemon() with NO_MM_FLAGS. Hence it does not set the
MM_NOCOUNTBIRTH flag which causes makemon() to invoke propagate() with the
argument that causes it not to increment the count of the number born.
Hence cleric summoning also extincts monsters.

You might as well assume that since weapons can be enchanted at +5 so can
armour.
